That would be why you call it a thought experiment, yes. Todays quantum
physicists would agree with you, but since this is partly a question of
interpretation of the formalism (as opposed to the formalism itself, which
always was easily understandable), it was something to think about in old
Erwin's times. Anyway, since the cat in the box _is_ part of NetHack, I
think it should keep in theme with the original thought experiment.


